1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
SGit × rUv Memory
A local MCP server. Encrypted checkpoints. Verified recovery.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
One interface. Four tools.
The client connects to the real MCP server over stdio.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Permission comes first.
Ruflo’s evaluator runs in enforce mode before checkpointing.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Two facts. One consistent snapshot.
SQLite backup captures committed data, including WAL writes.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
A real SGit vault commit.
Only the encrypted bare store leaves private staging.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Remove the source. Start fresh.
The demo removes the original database and restarts MCP.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Both facts are back.
Decrypt, verify the digest, check SQLite, then promote.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Tampering stops here.
The demo alters stored bytes, then tries another restore.

